abstract: >-
  Stage-2 Turkish<->Hindi speech-to-speech translation: a Cohere2 backbone
  (LoRA r=32, +MLP, rsLoRA) fused with a frozen Moshi depth decoder over Mimi
  codes, trained text+audio on a synthetic FLORES/OPUS-100/conversational
  corpus. The v0.3 long-horizon run covered 76,250 steps (2.07 epochs) on Cloud
  TPU v6e-16 provided by Google's TPU Research Cloud (TRC), reaching a best
  validation composite of 2.8199. The release evaluation frames the result as a
  data-efficiency study: the text inner-monologue learns to translate
  (free-run chrF++ ~25), while intelligible audio synthesis remains the
  frontier, bounded by the frozen depth decoder.
  LICENSE SCOPE - the Apache-2.0 license above applies to THIS SOURCE CODE
  only. The released model weights at the repository-artifact URL are
  CC-BY-NC-4.0 (non-commercial), inherited from the CC-BY-NC-4.0 base model
  CohereLabs/tiny-aya-base; the Moshi/Mimi components are CC-BY-4.0. See
  THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
